traceability.how_satisfied:
The dedicated parser implements WHATWG URL Standard section 5.1 exactly:
- split on "&" only;
- skip empty components;
- split at the first "=";
- convert "+" to a space;
- percent-decode as UTF-8;
- keep duplicates.
The validator collapses every non-conforming case into one invalid outcome. This covers a missing parameter, an empty value, an over-long value, non-letter characters, a repeated text parameter, extra parameters, a wrong-case name and an empty name. The response builder returns the constant HTTP 400 body {"error": "invalid_text"} with Content-Type application/json. All valid and invalid examples listed in the Requirement are traced in the Interfaces & Data Flows section and are covered by the verification suites. The deployment model requires intermediaries to forward the query string unmodified.
